course: dictionary
lesson: 12482
title: Delineated: marked out clearly
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Delineated means shown or marked out clearly, with the edges or limits easy to see. It can describe lines on a pitch, borders on a map, or rules that have been explained in detail. «The football pitch was delineated by white lines.» The white lines show exactly where the pitch begins and ends.
explain: Look for clue words in the sentence. Words like clearly, sharply and well often come before delineated, and they tell you the edges are easy to see. «The rules for the class trip were clearly delineated on the notice board.» Clearly tells you the rules were easy to understand.
explain: Test your meaning by swapping in a simpler phrase. «The map showed the border of each country, sharply delineated in red.» If "sharply marked out" fits in place of delineated and the sentence still makes sense, your meaning is right.
fact: Delineated is the past form of the verb delineate, so it describes something that has been marked out or explained.
fact: «Delineated» means described or explained clearly and in detail.
fact: «Delineated» can also mean marked out with lines or edges, so the limits are clear.
fact: In art, «delineated» means drawn or outlined, as in «a delineated shape».
fact: Phrases you may see are «clearly delineated», «sharply delineated» and «well delineated».
exercise: «The fields on the farm map were delineated by hedges.» What does delineated mean here? | Planted with flowers | Quickly forgotten | Covered in snow | *Marked out with clear edges
exercise: «The rules of the game were clearly delineated in the handbook.» What does clearly delineated suggest? | Changed every day | Hidden in a drawer | *Explained clearly and in detail | Written in a hurry and then lost
exercise: «She delineated the outline of the leaf in pencil.» What does delineated mean here? | Washed away | Ate a bite of | Painted over in red | *Drew the outline of
test: «The school grounds are sharply delineated by a tall fence.» What does sharply delineated suggest? | The boundary cannot be seen at all | The fence is falling down | The fence is secret | *The edges are easy to see
test: «Mia's notes clearly delineated each step of the science experiment.» What does clearly delineated mean? | Each step was left out | Each step was rushed and missed | Each step was painted red | *Each step was explained clearly
exam: «The diagram delineated the parts of a flower with neat labels and lines.» Which word is closest in meaning to delineated? | Confused | Scribbled | Hidden | *Labelled
